### Modrinth

- Project/data source: https://modrinth.com / https://api.modrinth.com
- Mod metadata and files belong to their respective authors and Modrinth.
- The launcher uses a single identifying User-Agent, respects the documented
  rate limit (≤300 requests/minute), downloads directly from `cdn.modrinth.com`,
  verifies `sha1`/`sha512`, does not re-host or mirror Modrinth files, and does
  not bundle them in the installer.
- Modrinth API usage is subject to Modrinth's terms; see
  `docs/02-compliance-security.md` §5.1.

### CurseForge

- P0 **does not call the CurseForge API** and contains **no CurseForge API key**.
  It only opens project pages in the browser and parses local pack zips.
- P1 may integrate CurseForge only with the operator's own official API key and
  after the legal prerequisites in `docs/02-compliance-security.md` §5.2
  (key not exposed in client, no API-data caching, no proxy anonymity,
  competitor-terms review) are satisfied.

### BMCLAPI / mirrors

- BMCLAPI is a third-party mirror service; mirrored files remain the property of
  their source sites. It is not an open-source service and provides no SLA.
- The launcher displays the active download source in the UI and logs it; the
  mirror can be disabled. The launcher does not re-package BMCLAPI as its own
  public API/mirror.

### Other services

- Microsoft/Xbox Live authentication endpoints are used only for the user's own
  Microsoft account, with the user's consent; tokens are stored encrypted with
  Electron `safeStorage` (DPAPI on Windows) where persistence is implemented.
- No telemetry is sent by this project.

